      <div class="seo-section">
        <h2>About This Motorcycle Gear Ratio Calculator</h2>
        <p>This motorcycle gear ratio calculator helps riders understand how gearing changes translate to real-world speed. Enter your sprocket sizes, tyre profile, and gear ratios to instantly see your estimated top speed in every gear.</p>
        <h2>What Is Gear Ratio?</h2>
        <p>The overall gear ratio of a motorcycle is determined by dividing the rear sprocket teeth by the front sprocket teeth. A higher number means more torque multiplication and stronger acceleration; a lower number means higher top speed at the cost of low-end pull.</p>
        <h2>How Sprocket Changes Affect Speed</h2>
        <p>Adding one tooth to the rear sprocket (or removing one from the front) lowers your overall ratio, increasing acceleration but reducing top speed. Removing a rear tooth does the opposite. Small changes have a surprisingly noticeable effect, especially in lower gears.</p>
